      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. That much metformin raises the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 1,700 mg/day.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- Another dose.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I can enter it with a note that you verified the dose."
      }
